{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\nError: unknown field 'parent_str' for schema 'decomp-summary'","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aef4f35022c1c0ee"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae0561e9e7817db7","agent_id":"aa20800bf1cd32bd6","session_id":"56d91365-9d63-408b-ab52-49c7dc5b096b","uuid":"4d7324d5-74b1-41ea-a1aa-1899fd013980","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:44:45.605Z","tool_use_result":"Error: Exit code 1\nError: unknown field 'parent_str' for schema 'decomp-summary'","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aef4f35022c1c0ee","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1f3a2f5c-2891-4ea2-8d8f-ef0c021bdae3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad66f856a1a05b21","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-aqeju_7g/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E001.md","content":"# Investigate workspace resolution feasibility in the artifacts-only server context\n\n## Description\n\nResolve whether MLflow workspace membership resolution can operate inside a server running in artifacts-only mode, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The MLflow tracking server already validates workspace membership for non-artifact operations through the existing auth plugin infrastructure; this investigation determines whether that same resolution chain functions (or can be made to function) when only the workspace provider is initialized, and whether artifact requests carry enough information to resolve the workspace that owns the requested artifact. The outcome determines the implementation approach for both the plugin workspace-resolution work and the server-side workspace-aware artifacts-only mode: if resolution is currently coupled to full server initialization, a refactoring plan is produced as part of the findings.\n\n## Questions to Resolve\n\n1. Does the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace store initialization and resolution path depend on tracking store or model registry store availability?\n2. Can the `kubernetes://` workspace store resolve experiment-to-workspace mappings when invoked outside the full tracking server initialization sequence?\n3. Do artifact requests handled by the artifacts-only server (endpoints under `/api/2.0/mlflow/artifacts/*`) carry sufficient identifiers — experiment ID or run ID — to resolve the parent experiment and its workspace assignment, including for the S3 artifact store's `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` path structure?\n\n## Scope\n\n- Trace the MLflow server initialization sequence for `--artifacts-only` and for `--enable-workspaces` individually, and identify what breaks when both are set.\n- Trace the `WorkspaceStoreRegistry` / `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry-point loading path in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins and enumerate its initialization dependencies.\n- Determine the artifact request → parent experiment → workspace resolution chain, including how artifact request paths map to experiment IDs for the standard S3 artifact layout; document limitations for non-standard artifact roots.\n- Exercise the resolution chain locally where possible (the server and plugin are pip-installable; workspace store interactions may use test doubles or a lightweight API server).\n- Produce a findings report with a pass/fail answer and evidence for each question.\n- If workspace resolution is coupled to full server initialization, produce a refactoring plan that factors resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Each of the three questions above has a documented pass/fail answer with code-level evidence (file/function references or a reproducible local run).\n- The initialization dependency set of the plugin's workspace resolution is enumerated: what it requires and what it does not.\n- If coupling to tracking/model registry store initialization exists, the refactoring plan identifies the specific initialization path to decouple and the affected plugin surfaces; if no coupling exists, that is documented with evidence.\n- The artifact-path-to-experiment resolution is demonstrated (or its failure documented) for the S3-standard `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` layout.\n- Limitations for non-standard artifact root configurations are documented.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Enables HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3 (P0): the answers determine the implementation approach for workspace-validated, fail-closed artifact serving in the MLflow server.\n- Enables HLR-7 (P1): the answer determines whether the auth plugin workspace resolution requires refactoring for the artifacts-only context.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":78062,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae0561e9e7817db7","agent_id":"aa20800bf1cd32bd6","session_id":"56d91365-9d63-408b-ab52-49c7dc5b096b","uuid":"28cc1a0f-d6a8-4543-9962-2d420bdbdb6b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:44:53.221Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
