{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-bde8f85b-3692-46ff-9b4b-207496a65640","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf0585e9d064ec90","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-aqeju_7g/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E003.md","content":"# Artifacts-only workspace resolution in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\n\n## Description\n\nVerify and extend the kubernetes-auth plugin's workspace resolution so it functions correctly in the MLflow server's artifacts-only context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The plugin, registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`, already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking server's non-artifact operations; this epic makes that resolution available to the artifacts-only server. If the workspace resolution feasibility investigation finds the resolution path coupled to full tracking server initialization, this epic refactors it into an independent initialization path within the plugin. The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` authentication setup are unchanged — authentication at the ingress level works identically for both server modes.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Verify the plugin's workspace resolution (workspace store initialization, experiment-to-workspace lookup) in the artifacts-only server context, per the feasibility investigation's findings.\n- If the resolution path is coupled to tracking/model registry store initialization, factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path usable when only the workspace provider is initialized.\n- Preserve the plugin's existing behavior for the full tracking server — no regression to non-artifact workspace operations.\n- Unit and local integration tests covering workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context (workspace store accessed without tracking stores).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The plugin resolves experiment-to-workspace mappings in a server context where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized, demonstrated by automated tests.\n- Workspace resolution initialization does not require tracking store or model registry store availability.\n- The plugin's existing workspace resolution for the full tracking server is unchanged (regression tests pass).\n- Any refactoring indicated by the feasibility investigation's findings is implemented and covered by tests.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P1, direct): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization.\n- Enables HLR-2 and HLR-3 (P0): the server's workspace validation and fail-closed denial depend on this resolution capability; priority inherits P0 through that enablement.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":81714,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae0561e9e7817db7","agent_id":"aa20800bf1cd32bd6","session_id":"56d91365-9d63-408b-ab52-49c7dc5b096b","uuid":"94c85ade-a22e-45ec-8b6e-1897d90d7f6b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:45:31.326Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
