{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aff4be545f2d3294","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: Split-server artifacts-only topology in the MLflow operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the tracking server requires a delegation configuration (outcome\n15\t    B), the routing design shifts from pure gateway-level HTTPRoute routing to also\n16\t    configuring server-side delegation, revising the chart templates and main-deployment\n17\t    configuration.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Split-server artifacts-only topology in the MLflow operator\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, forming a split-server topology: the main tracking deployment handles experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry, while the dedicated instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation. The operator propagates workspace configuration to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration mechanisms it already uses for the main tracking deployment, and configures the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the dedicated instance, per the routing mechanism selected by the artifact traffic routing investigation. This is a split-server topology, not a single-deployment configuration flag (Staff Engineer / SME input).\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute, following the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern (MLflow CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, applied via Server-Side Apply).\n44\t- MLflow CR spec extension to express the split-server artifact serving configuration and its conversion to Helm values.\n45\t- Propagate workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same mechanisms as the main tracking deployment; the artifacts-only Deployment runs with the flag combination `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`.\n46\t- Configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the dedicated instance, per the routing mechanism investigation's outcome (gateway-level HTTPRoute routing and/or tracking-deployment configuration).\n47\t- Gateway API HTTPRoute resources created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n48\t- kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment.\n49\t- Operator validation that rejects MLflow CR configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks workspace flags — misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation.\n50\t- Extend the chart so the second Deployment requires no structural change to the chart architecture (strategy assumption; escalate as a risk if found false during implementation).\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, reconciliation creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment, measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n55\t- The rendered artifacts-only Deployment container command includes `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`, measured by inspecting the container command in the rendered Deployment spec.\n56\t- Artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated instance is configured per the selected routing mechanism and verified in a test cluster (routing verification is against the routing configuration itself and does not depend on the workspace-aware server capability; any server image may be used).\n57\t- Invalid MLflow CR configurations — an artifacts-only instance without workspace flags — are rejected with a clear validation error.\n58\t- Existing single-deployment MLflow CRs reconcile unchanged when split-server configuration is absent (no regression).\n59\t- HTTPRoute creation follows the existing conditional CRD discovery pattern for Gateway API.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-5 (P1): MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n64\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0e03bcdde289170","agent_id":"ae9b5f452b559db63","session_id":"56d91365-9d63-408b-ab52-49c7dc5b096b","uuid":"09816555-4654-48ba-927c-cb9646207690","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:47:50.838Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aff4be545f2d3294","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
