king-server configuration that delegates artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, per the mechanism specified by the routing investigation.\n43\t- Ensure existing MLflow clients remain compatible: artifact endpoint resolution behavior is documented and preserved where possible.\n44\t- The configuration is absent/disabled by default; deployments without the split-server topology retain current artifact-serving behavior.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- With the delegation configuration set, artifact operations handled by the main tracking server are directed to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n49\t- Without the delegation configuration, the tracking server's artifact-serving behavior is unchanged.\n50\t- The configuration surface is documented so the operator can manage it declaratively through the MLflow CR.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance — the server-side half of the routing mechanism, conditional on the routing investigation's outcome B.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0e03bcdde289170","agent_id":"ae9b5f452b559db63","session_id":"56d91365-9d63-408b-ab52-49c7dc5b096b","uuid":"f1f09f2e-93d7-4da5-9f3c-7abbf9266ab4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:47:51.517Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9af38817e91bd214","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
