l roots with no shared deliverable — correct. Critical path length 3 (E001→E003→E004) is within the M-strategy heuristic (3-4). No E004↔E005 edge: the operator's chart templates reference the server's flag combination as configuration, gated by the rendered-container-command AC on E005 — the rule-compliant Rule 13/14 shape, correctly not an artifact edge; the routing-verification AC explicitly decouples verification from the workspace-aware server capability. No konflux-onboarding/repo-onboarding/license-validation epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism is not applicable. Branch file BRANCH-B-E006 correctly sets both `branch: B` (matching the filename) and `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002`, which also appears in its `dependencies`. No main-plan epic lists a branch epic in `dependencies` — E005 correctly depends on the Investigation (E002) itself, with the outcome-B coupling to E006 expressed as an AC-gated configuration reference. No data/artifact dependency discoverable from epic content is missing from the DAG.\n23\t\n24\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n25\tAll epics carry `component: MLflow` / `team: MLflow Team`, with the non-canonical strategy components (MLflow Operator, mlflow-kubernetes-plugins) mapped to canonical `MLflow` and the mapping documented in the summary — the only team is MLflow Team, so no cross-team bundling exists. E005 is above the ~2-week guideline (2-3 sprints) but is one logical change (CR spec → Helm values → rendered split topology) with estimate, rationale, and a concrete conditional re-split trigger all present in Health Warnings — watch item only, no dock. No scope duplication across siblings: E003 (plugin resolution), E004 (server validation), E005 (operator topology), and E006 (server delegation config) touch distinct surfaces. No work-product type mixing (no content authoring bundled with code).\n26\t\n27\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n28\tBoth Investigations genuinely resolve uncertainty that changes downstream structure: E001's outcome determines whether E003 is verification-only or a refactoring and shapes E004's validation approach; E002's outcome determines whether BRANCH-B-E006 exists at all. All four Implementation epics produce concrete artifacts (plugin code + tests, server code, chart templates, server configuration). Gating metadata is complete and correct: every epic with `gated_by` has `gate_failure_impact` populated with both `action` and a substantive `fallback_approach` (E003/E004: rewrite; E005: rewrite; E006: remove); every epic listing an Investigation in `dependencies` has `gated_by` set; every `gated_by` target appears in that epic's direct `dependencies` list.\n29\t\n30\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n31\tSignal fields are type-correct: E001/E002 carry `investigation_signals` (5-signal rubric); E003/E004/E005/BRANCH-B-E006 carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric). All six ai-signals rationale files exist, and the rationale tables match the frontmatter values exactly. Signal values are consistent with the strategy content: E001's high local runnability is justified by pip-installability of the server and plugin; E002's lower local runnability / cluster dependence reflects that end-to-end gateway validation needs a cluster while the decision itself is source-determinable; E003's `change_specificity: 0` and `open_questions: -1` correctly reflect the approach being undetermined until E001 reports. Architecture-claims calibration verified against `.context`: the strategy's premises (kubernetes-auth plugin v1.5.0 via `--app-name kubernetes-auth`, `--enable-workspaces` with `kubernetes://` workspace store, Dockerfile.konflux CMD including `--serve-artifacts`, operator Helm-in-operator with conditional Gateway API CRD discovery) are corroborated by `mlflow.md` and `mlflow-operator.md`, and all four Implementation epics score `architecture_claims: 1` with rationales citing those files — no calibration miss.\n32\t\n33\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n34\tEvery epic